 the Lightsail instance running n8n and Chatwoot (read-only IAM policy), in the region of the server.","validate":null},{"id":"chatwoot","title":"Chatwoot API token and account id","who":"developer","stores":"vault:one_chatwoot_token + settings.chatwoot.account_id","unblocks":["WITTY-03","WITTY-05","HB chatwoot","T-WITTY-TURN"],"how":"Chatwoot → Profile settings → Access token. Save it as one_chatwoot_token; the account id is in Settings → Chatwoot.","validate":"chatwoot"},{"id":"vercel","title":"Vercel token for the eduwit team","who":"developer","stores":"vault:one_vercel_token","unblocks":["WEB-07","HB vercel:website","HB vercel:one"],"how":"Vercel → Account settings → Tokens → Create, scoped to the eduwit team, read access. Save it as one_vercel_token.","validate":"vercel"},{"id":"spark_job_key","title":"Spark base URL and b2c_internal_key (b2c.app_deploy_set)","who":"developer","stores":"b2c.settings app.base_url + vault:b2c_internal_key","unblocks":["PLAT-05 (b2c part)","HB spark","FIX-OUTBOX-B2C"],"how":"Spark's own setting, filled in Spark: select b2c.app_deploy_set('https://spark.eduwit.in', '<B2C_INTERNAL_KEY from Vercel eduwit-spark>'). Eduwit One only reads it (PLAT-05).","validate":"plat05"},{"id":"b2b_app","title":"B2B CRM host and a read API key (target: referrals-only)","who":"developer","stores":"settings.hosts.b2b_app + vault:one_b2b_read_key","unblocks":["HB b2b-app","Apps / B2B deep links"],"how":"The B2B CRM host (Settings → Hosts → b2b_app) and a referrals-only API key from the B2B CRM's Settings → API keys, saved as one_b2b_read_key.","validate":"health:b2b_app"},{"id":"website_health","title":"Website public health endpoint","who":"developer","stores":"settings.hosts.website","unblocks":["WEB-02","HB website"],"how":"The website's address (Settings → Hosts → website). Its /api/health must answer.","validate":"health:website"},{"id":"influencer_portal","title":"Influencer portal host and health endpoint","who":"developer","stores":"settings.hosts.influencer","unblocks":["INF-04","HB influencer"],"how":"The influencer portal's address (Settings → Hosts → influencer). Its /api/health must answer.","validate":"health:influencer"},{"id":"whatsapp","title":"WhatsApp system-user token and WABA ids","who":"developer","stores":"vault:one_whatsapp_token + settings.whatsapp.waba_ids","unblocks":["B2C-06 (template and quality parts)","HB whatsapp:witty","HB whatsapp:b2c"],"how":"Meta Business → System users → generate a token with whatsapp_business_management, saved as one_whatsapp_token; the WABA ids go in Settings → WhatsApp.","validate":"whatsapp"},{"id":"meta","title":"Meta ad-account read token","who":"developer","stores":"vault:one_meta_token","unblocks":["HB meta","Marketing spend tiles"],"how":"A Meta ad-account read token, saved as one_meta_token, for the spend tiles on the Marketing page.","validate":null},{"id":"email","title":"Email provider for alerts (Resend)","who":"developer","stores":"vault:one_email_key","unblocks":["alert delivery","T-ALERT"],"how":"Resend → API keys → Create (sending access, domain eduwit.in), saved as one_email_key. Validate sends a test email to the P1 inbox.","validate":"email"},{"id":"uptimerobot","title":"UptimeRobot read-only API key (external watchdog)","who":"developer","stores":"vault:one_uptimerobot_key","unblocks":["watchdog for one:tick and one:app","HB from external monitors"],"how":"UptimeRobot → Integrations & API → Main API key (read-only is enough), saved as one_uptimerobot_key.","validate":"uptimerobot"},{"id":"ai_key","title":"Anthropic API key for the AI layer (Claude only)","who":"owner","stores":"vault:one_anthropic_key","unblocks":["classify","triage","explain","propose_fix","propose_feature","brief","ask","test_author"],"how":"An Anthropic API key from the Claude Console (console.anthropic.com → API keys), saved here as one_anthropic_key. Claude only (owner, 24 Oct). The model and price of each tier are in Settings → AI; a model without a price is never called. Validate checks every tier's model, and the refusal fallback, with a free model lookup.","validate":"ai"},{"id":"sentry","title":"Sentry","who":"owner","stores":"none","unblocks":[],"how":"Not used: monitoring is UptimeRobot (owner, 23 Oct).","validate":null},{"id":"alerts_p1_inbox","title":"P1 email inbox","who":"owner","stores":"settings.alerts.p1.email","unblocks":["P1 delivery"],"how":"Where P1 alerts go. Settings → Alerts → P1 email (owner only). Validate sends a test email.","validate":"email"},{"id":"alerts_second_contact","title":"Second P1 contact (60 min unacknowledged)","who":"owner","stores":"settings.alerts.escalation.second_contact","unblocks":["second-level escalation"],"how":"Who gets the 60-minute escalation. Settings → Alerts → second contact (owner only).","validate":null},{"id":"developer_contact","title":"Developer email and GitHub handle","who":"owner","stores":"settings.alerts.developer_email","unblocks":["developer-tagged alerts","GitHub issues"],"how":"Who gets developer-tagged alerts (failing function, migration drift, privilege audit, Vercel build). Settings → Alerts → developer email.","validate":null},{"id":"test_whatsapp_number","title":"Real test WhatsApp number in w2_trusted (is_test), with its own sender","who":"developer","stores":"settings.test_identities.whatsapp_number + settings.test_identities.whatsapp_phone_number_id + settings.test_identities.witty_number + vault:one_test_wa_token","unblocks":["T-WITTY-TURN"],"how":"Add the test number to w2_trusted with is_test = true (Witty's admin). Register it on a WhatsApp Business account Eduwit One may send from: Settings → test_identities: whatsapp_number (digits), whatsapp_phone_number_id (the sender's Graph id), witty_number (Witty's number, digits); paste the sender's token here. WhatsApp lets a business number send free text only within 24 hours of the other side's last message: Witty's replies keep that window open while T-WITTY-TURN runs; after a longer pause, send one message to the test number from Witty's side, or the send step fails.","validate":"test_whatsapp"},{"id":"test_mailbox","title":"Test mailbox that receives website codes and alert tests","who":"developer","stores":"settings.test_identities.mailbox + vault:one_test_mailbox_key","unblocks":["T-WEB-ENQUIRY","T-ALERT"],"how":"A mailbox the tests can read, for enquiry and alert journeys. Settings → Test identities, key as one_test_mailbox_key.","validate":null},{"id":"test_preview_url","title":"Website preview URL with Turnstile test keys","who":"developer","stores":"settings.test_identities.website_preview_url","unblocks":["T-WEB-ENQUIRY","T-WEB-ADVISOR"],"how":"A website preview deployment the tests may submit forms to. Settings → Test identities.","validate":null},{"id":"test_spark_user","title":"Spark user marked is_test_user (the test runner login can be it)","who":"developer","stores":"settings.test_identities.spark_test_user_email","unblocks":["T-HANDOFF","T-B2C-NURTURE"],"how":"The test runner login (test_runner_user) covers this when it is a Spark admin with is_test_user; Spark gives test leads only to test users or admins.","validate":null},{"id":"test_b2b_intake_key","title":"B2B API key scoped to intake for test leads","who":"developer","stores":"vault:one_b2b_intake_key","unblocks":["T-B2B-INTAKE","T-B2B-PUSH","T-HANDOFF"],"how":"A B2B CRM intake-only API key for test leads, saved as one_b2b_intake_key.","validate":"b2b_intake"},{"id":"test_partner","title":"Test partner with a sandbox endpoint and an inbound secret","who":"developer","stores":"settings.test_identities.partner_slug + vault:one_test_partner_secret","unblocks":["T-B2B-PUSH"],"how":"In the B2B CRM add a partner used only for tests, with test_endpoint set to a sandbox you control (https) and an inbound secret; it must be the only partner with a test_endpoint, or the push test refuses to run. Settings → test_identities.partner_slug; paste the inbound secret here.","validate":"test_partner"},{"id":"test_creator","title":"Test creator with a known referral code","who":"developer","stores":"settings.test_identities.creator_referral_code","unblocks":["T-INFLUENCER"],"how":"An influencer-portal creator marked as a test creator, with a referral code. Settings → Test identities.","validate":null},{"id":"test_rows_agreement","title":"Owner agreement to create and purge test rows in production","who":"owner","stores":"docs/DECISIONS.md","unblocks":["all synthetic tests"],"how":"Agreed on 23 Oct: test rows may be created in production under the is_test conventions and purged nightly.","validate":null},{"id":"brand_assets","title":"Eduwit logo and colour palette","who":"owner","stores":"web/public/brand","unblocks":["UI theme","alert email wordmark"],"how":"The Eduwit logo and palette. An SVG wordmark would replace the PNGs (question Q6).","validate":null},{"id":"supabase_api_schema","title":"Expose schema one in the Supabase API (Project settings → Data API → Exposed schemas: add one)","who":"owner","stores":"supabase project setting","unblocks":["the app's reads and writes","HTTP probes","/api/watchdog"],"how":"Supabase → Project settings → Data API → Exposed schemas: add one, save. The app and this page read through it.","validate":"api_schema"},{"id":"one_app_env","title":"Eduwit One app environment: ONE_SUPABASE_URL, ONE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, ONE_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY and ONE_INTERNAL_KEY in Vercel; the same key as Vault one_internal_key; one.settings.app.base_url; the sign-in redirect URL","who":"developer","stores":"vercel env + vault:one_internal_key + one.settings.app","unblocks":["HB one:app","HTTP probes (WEB-02, WEB-07, INF-04, WITTY-05)","PLAT-05 (one part)"],"how":"Vercel project eduwit-one, Production env: ONE_SUPABASE_URL, ONE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, ONE_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY, ONE_INTERNAL_KEY (the same value as Vault one_internal_key). Then Settings → App → base_url = https://one.eduwit.in, and in Supabase → Authentication → URL configuration add https://one.eduwit.in/auth/callback.","validate":"app_link"},{"id":"watchdog_monitor","title":"UptimeRobot keyword monitor on https://one.eduwit.in/api/watchdog with an active alert contact (docs/RUNBOOK.md)","who":"owner","stores":"uptimerobot","unblocks":["notice when Supabase, pg_cron or Vercel is down"],"how":"UptimeRobot keyword monitor on https://one.eduwit.in/api/watchdog for \"ok\":true, every 5 minutes, alert contact active (docs/RUNBOOK.md).","validate":"watchdog"},{"id":"test_runner_user","title":"Test runner login: a B2B admin with two-factor and a Spark admin, used only by the synthetic tests","who":"owner","stores":"settings.test_identities.runner_email + vault:one_test_runner_password + vault:one_test_runner_totp","unblocks":["T-B2B-INTAKE","T-B2B-PUSH","T-HANDOFF","T-B2C-NURTURE","the purge of B2B and Spark test leads"],"how":"Create a Supabase user for the tests (for example tests@eduwit.in, agreed with the CRM owner, S-21). In the B2B CRM make it an admin with two-factor required and enrol a TOTP factor; in Spark make it an admin with is_test_user. Settings → test_identities.runner_email; paste its password and the TOTP secret (base32) here. Eduwit One signs in as it, with the one-time code, only to route, log and delete test leads (D-070).","validate":"test_runner"},{"id":"test_spark_journey","title":"A Spark journey in test mode for the nurture test","who":"owner","stores":"settings.test_identities.spark_test_journey_id","unblocks":["T-B2C-NURTURE"],"how":"In Spark, create a journey in test mode whose first step queues a WhatsApp message; Settings → test_identities.spark_test_journey_id.","validate":"spark_journey"},{"id":"catalogue_engine","title":"Catalogue Engine installed in this database (schema ce)","who":"developer","stores":"none (reads schema ce of the shared database)","unblocks":["CE-01","CE-02","CE-03","CE-04","CE-05","events from ce.events"],"how":"Nothing to paste. Once the Catalogue Engine's migrations are applied to this database (production: after 1 Nov 2026, from the engine's own repository), press Validate: it checks that ce.heartbeat, ce.job, ce.health, ce.run and ce.events exist with the columns Eduwit One reads and that the database owner can read them, then switches on CE-01 to CE-05. The event copy from ce.events starts by itself as soon as the table exists.","validate":"engine_schema"}]}$seed$::jsonb, 'seed', 'seed: generated config');
